WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.360
This video shows what SWATrust lets you set
for a run, and where each setting goes.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.140
SWATrust runs a copy of the model.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:12.560
It writes your settings into the copy and
does not change the folder of the model.

00:00:13.061 --> 00:00:15.966
In Set-up, click Clear choice and tick the
model,

00:00:15.966 --> 00:00:18.101
so that it is the only model chosen.

00:00:18.301 --> 00:00:20.251
Type the first year and press Enter.

00:00:20.451 --> 00:00:22.011
Do the same for the last year.

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:35.180
Type the number of warm-up years and press
Enter.

00:00:35.681 --> 00:00:38.584
The line under the three boxes says how
many years

00:00:38.584 --> 00:00:41.371
run and for which years the model holds
weather.

00:00:41.571 --> 00:00:45.151
The warm-up years are simulated, but not
written to the tables.

00:00:45.652 --> 00:00:49.466
A period that the model cannot run is
refused in the same line,

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:51.282
with the years to choose from.

00:00:55.357 --> 00:01:01.113
The column Output tables has one row for
each table and one box for each time step:

00:01:01.113 --> 00:01:03.957
Day, Mon, Year and Avg, the average year.

00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:07.049
Tick a box to write that table at that
time step.

00:01:08.649 --> 00:01:10.589
Clear a box to leave the table out.

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:15.259
The page opens with the ticks of the
model's own tables.

00:01:15.459 --> 00:01:18.439
SWATrust adds one tick and says so under
the list.

00:01:18.639 --> 00:01:22.018
The tick is the daily water balance of the
entire basin,

00:01:22.018 --> 00:01:24.189
from which Results draws its charts.

00:01:24.389 --> 00:01:26.889
Some rows have boxes that cannot be
ticked.

00:01:27.391 --> 00:01:28.943
Under Calibrated values,

00:01:28.943 --> 00:01:33.211
the page names the file of calibrated
values that the run applies.

00:01:33.411 --> 00:01:35.551
To run with another file, click Choose.

00:01:35.751 --> 00:01:39.441
Calibrate and validate writes such a file
of fitted values.

00:01:39.943 --> 00:01:41.474
To change any other input,

00:01:41.474 --> 00:01:46.067
change it in a copy of the model with the
tools that you built the model with,

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:48.953
and add the copy as Run your own model
describes.
